                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                        "entry_id": "7a14016a-afc1-3b14-b49d-d887608832b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "imię żeńskie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10b542a3-81dc-48a0-8ca5-4d8d46cad48d",
                                "sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                                "text": "Mam na imię Łucja i jestem aktorką z Wrocławia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21dc046a-cda0-4ad4-9f3c-e8c3f2dd90fc",
                                "sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                                "text": "Łucja Prus śpiewała piosenki, które na długo pozostają w pamięci"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2edb585f-3a37-4400-9380-e76191aebe12",
                                "sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                                "text": "W Kościele katolickim na 13 grudnia przypada wspomnienie św. Łucji z Syrakuz, patronki niewidomych, chorych na oczy, pisarzy i poetów."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b253383-07e1-4df9-8b64-5656d11b33f7",
                                "sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                                "text": "Łucje dzień swej patronki, czyli imieniny, obchodzą 13 grudnia, a także 25 czerwca i 9 lipca."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2dedca00-48ca-48a2-bdae-c33ceac23222",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a14016a-afc1-3b14-b49d-d887608832b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dfd9304-8dc9-3bcf-96a7-ed3636ed250a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lucy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lucy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbac1faa-24d8-3f5f-bc50-72db95a30473",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from Latin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "351d7fe4-c309-42fd-ae30-c0b05c709948",
                                                "sense_id": "dbac1faa-24d8-3f5f-bc50-72db95a30473",
                                                "text": "Then did my younger brother Amidas / Love that same other Damzell, Lucy bright, / To whom but little dowre allotted was; / Her vertue was the dowre, that did delight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c721ddbb-cf04-4d7f-aeae-355b948eaec1",
                                                "sense_id": "dbac1faa-24d8-3f5f-bc50-72db95a30473",
                                                "text": "She liv'd unknown, and few could know / When Lucy ceas'd to be; / But she is in her Grave, and, Oh ! / The difference to me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9e954a0-4566-49de-85e7-cdad42a1ce14",
                                                "sense_id": "dbac1faa-24d8-3f5f-bc50-72db95a30473",
                                                "text": "But certainly there are some names which seem to belong to particular classes of character, to form the mind and even influence the destiny: Louisa, now; - is not your Louisa necessarily a die-away damsel, who reads novels, and holds her head on one side, languishing and given to love! Is not Lucy a pretty soubrette, a wearer of cast gowns and cast smiles, smart and coquettish!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "132314ee-3a7c-4ca8-98c7-6f491c121cbb",
                                                "sense_id": "dbac1faa-24d8-3f5f-bc50-72db95a30473",
                                                "text": "Now we'll just use a fiction name / Lucy that sounds nice / A name we can remember / Without repeating twice / / My name is so old fashioned / And they are very few / But some will have a puzzled look / And whisper Lucy who?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c9657ce-abf9-3a99-a957-a43ad2b9b732",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname from Old French derived from place names in Normandy based on a male personal name, from Latin Lucius."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf4105a-39d0-49b4-87c4-40a47dd592e9",
                                                "sense_id": "0c9657ce-abf9-3a99-a957-a43ad2b9b732",
                                                "text": "Here is Sir William Lucy, who with me / Set from our o'ermatch'd forces forth for aid."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a92cc25-6ab9-351a-b272-43b036a0ad8a",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fossilized partial skeleton of a female Australopithecus afarensis discovered in Ethiopia, an early hominin; also, the individual whose skeleton this was."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8efe8e8-10bd-4d9e-a482-4545d88c8533",
                                                "sense_id": "0a92cc25-6ab9-351a-b272-43b036a0ad8a",
                                                "text": "A new analysis of Lucy’s bones suggests that she may have fallen to her death from a tall tree. […] In 1974, scientists working in Ethiopia uncovered an extraordinary female skeleton, whom they called Lucy. She was 3.2 million years old, and belonged to a new species of hominid now known as Australopithecus afarensis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a912d46-f5a3-3c3e-ac33-6e5d97ebbc91",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place name:",
                                            "A village in Montmort-Lucy commune, Marne department, Grand Est, France."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d76f4f78-de71-3ba6-914b-be70d1f6bf2e",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place name:",
                                            "A commune in Moselle department, Grand Est, France."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "054ca973-de69-3ee7-b065-14f1d1c081f4",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place name:",
                                            "A commune in Seine-Maritime department, Normandy, France."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "723433bc-6bd9-3dfd-8f1c-30f5c4e8724b",
                                        "entry_id": "2090b38a-774c-3b4e-ab53-2afdf7bae8d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place name:",
                                            "An unincorporated community in Houston County, Alabama, United States."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lucy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc308d11-1211-3222-a9ae-23c614630272",
                                        "entry_id": "0e256e4a-2eac-3920-a789-d711165506f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The drug LSD."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75c38c2f-c34b-40b0-ba80-52596fa7432e",
                                                "sense_id": "cc308d11-1211-3222-a9ae-23c614630272",
                                                "text": "Picture yourself in a boat on a river/With tangerine trees and marmalade skies/Somebody calls you, you answer quite slowly/A girl with kaleidoscope eyes/Cellophane flowers of yellow and green/Towering over your head/Look for the girl with the sun in her eyes/And she's gone/Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81113b71-6450-4cc5-9f4a-e921782cdbec",
                                                "sense_id": "cc308d11-1211-3222-a9ae-23c614630272",
                                                "text": "The last time I made moocah, or dug sweet Lucy, was with Janis Joplin, who gave me one that must have been rolled by Montezuma himself. I saw my thoughts in clear letters, and they both felt and looked like a double strike on a coin […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb976ce8-d65a-4e46-904a-d65e3f1398fe",
                                                "sense_id": "cc308d11-1211-3222-a9ae-23c614630272",
                                                "text": "Tanya shook her head slowly. 'We married to fill out the missing bits of ourselves. That doesn't have to be a bad reason. But you see, I'd been \"in it\". The contrast between that infernal blaze of feeling and keep-the-home-fires burning was just too much. It's why one mustn't start taking Lucy. Lucy was the current slang for LSD."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
